  "title": "More control over generated video",
  "summary": "This week gave builders more control over video and images while making the surrounding APIs, usage records, and dashboard less surprising.\n\nSupported video models now accept both a start image and an end image, while a single image still works as before. Seedance-pro gained dimension-aware framing across seven aspect ratios, with output limited to 720p. Model listings now expose video capabilities, and the MCP video tool accepts longer durations where the model supports them.\n\nSeedream 5 gained multiple reference images and aspect-ratio inference for edits; Seedream 4.0 gained custom dimensions. Seedream 4.0, 4.5 Pro, and 5 moved to Replicate without changing their public model IDs. Paid-only Gemini 3.5 Flash joined the lineup with multimodal input and a 1,048,576-token context window. Image-capability listings were also corrected, and chat now returns a clear 400 when a selected model cannot accept an image.\n\nAssemblyAI and ElevenLabs Scribe can return speaker-labeled, timestamped transcripts through `response_format=diarized_json`. Per-request usage records and CSV exports gained separate input-audio, output-audio, and output-video seconds, with fractional video durations in generation events. Pricing now derives Pollen charges from one cost rate per model; Gemini Fast input-audio and Scribe hourly charges changed.\n\nSeveral fixed time limits were removed from slower gateway and image-fetching paths, and AssemblyAI transcription polling now allows up to four minutes. An unconfigured usage rate no longer prevents other rated usage in the same report from being tracked and charged. Provider rate limits now return a 502 from the text API while retaining the upstream status for debugging. The `/api/docs` redirect also preserves query parameters, including `?format=json`.",
